Subject: Health files for the app

The firmware writes two small text files in its folder, for the Health window
of the app. health.txt holds the battery, the charge state, the runtime
counters, and on models with ATA storage the identify block and the SMART
block of the disk, as hexadecimal digits. It is written when the computer is
about to get the disk, after the settings are saved, and at a clean power off
or restart, except on a hard disk with a flat battery, where nothing is
written. charge.txt holds the battery level and voltage at the moment the
charger was unplugged; an unplug seen while the computer holds the disk is
kept in memory and written once the disk is back, and one seen in the early
USB screen of the start-up is written once the settings are loaded. Both files
are written whole and never read back. Nothing is shown on the iPod.

